{"name":"C’est la Vie","hex":"#83bce5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"c’est la vie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["An expression of acceptance of misfortune in life; that's life; such is life; so it goes"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/c%E2%80%99est_la_vie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glossary of French words and expressions in English","blocks":[{"text":"Many words in the English language are of French origin (\"gallicism\"s). Most of them came from the Anglo-Norman spoken by the upper classes in England for several hundred years after the Norman Conquest, before the language settled into what became Modern English. English words of French origin, such as art, competition, force, money, and table are pronounced according to English rules of phonology, rather than French, and English speakers commonly use them without any awareness of their French origin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_French_words_and_expressions_in_English","wikidata":"Q21067567"},{"title":"C'est la Vie (comic strip)","blocks":[{"text":"C'est la Vie is a comic strip by Jennifer Babcock. Since November 11, 2003, the strip has been syndicated on the web by Uclick/Universal Uclick/Andrews McMeel Syndication."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C'est_la_Vie_(comic_strip)","wikidata":"Q5005809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Aperitif_for_five.jpg/500px-Aperitif_for_five.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Aperitif_for_five.jpg/1280px-Aperitif_for_five.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Aperitif_for_five.jpg/500px-Aperitif_for_five.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apéritifs with amuse-gueules","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o